# Markdown tables

Every Markdown/GFM table MUST be visually aligned in the source:

- Pad every cell with spaces so columns line up in a monospace editor.
- The separator row (`---`) must be the same width as the padded cells (including the spaces around cell text).
- Do not leave ragged tables like `| Foo | Bar |` on one row and `| something long | x |` on the next.

Example:

```markdown
| Kind       | What                          |
|------------|-------------------------------|
| Posts      | Four page bundles with covers |
| Co-speaker | One talk lists Jordan Blake   |
```

Not:

```markdown
| Kind | What |
| ---- | ---- |
| Posts | Four page bundles with covers |
| Co-speaker | One talk lists Jordan Blake |
```
